nese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Wu Ju-lun\">Wu Ju-lun</a></div><div class=\"wst-header-forward-arrow\">\u2192</div></div></div><div class=\"wst-header-notes header&#95;notes searchaux wst-unknown-notes\"><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r14791120\">.mw-parser-output .plainSister{display:block;font-size:93%;line-height:normal;list-style-type:none;list-style-image:none;list-style-position:outside;border:1px solid var(--border-color-interactive--hover,#AAA);float:right;clear:right;margin:0.5ex 0 0.5ex 0.5ex;padding:0;background:var(--background-color-base,#FFFFFF);color:var(--color-base,#202122)}.mw-parser-output .sisicon,.mw-parser-output .dabicon{padding-right:1ex}</style><ul class=\"plainSister\"><li class=\"sisitem\"><span class=\"sisicon\"><span typeof=\"mw:File/Frameless\"><a href=\"/wiki/Special:SiteMatrix\" title=\"Special:SiteMatrix\"><img alt=\"Sister Projects\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Wikimedia-logo.svg/20px-Wikimedia-logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikisource.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Wikimedia-logo.svg/40px-Wikimedia-logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikisource.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1024\" data-file-height=\"1024\" /></a></span></span><a href=\"/wiki/Special:SiteMatrix\" title=\"Special:SiteMatrix\">sister projects</a>: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wu_Renchen\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Wu Renchen\">Wikipedia article</a>, <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q107367895\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"d:Q107367895\">Wikidata item</a></li></ul></div><div class=\"ws-noexport\" id=\"ws-data\" style=\"speak:none\"><span id=\"ws-article-id\">3675198</span><span id=\"ws-title\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period\">Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period</a>, Volume 2 \u2014 Wu J\u00ean-ch&#39;\u00ean</span><span id=\"ws-editor\">Arthur W. Hummel</span><span id=\"ws-author\">Tu Lien-ch\u00ea</span></div></div>\n<p><span style=\"display:none\" id=\"dynamic&#95;layout&#95;overrider\">Layout 2</span>\n</p>\n<div class=\"prp-pages-output\" lang=\"en\">\n<p><span><span class=\"pagenum ws-pagenum\" id=\"870\" data-page-number=\"870\" data-page-name=\"Page:Eminent Chinese Of The Ch\u2019ing Period - Hummel - 1943 - Vol. 2.pdf/268\" data-page-index=\"268\" data-page-quality=\"3\" title=\"Page:Eminent&#95;Chinese&#95;Of&#95;The&#95;Ch%E2%80%99ing&#95;Period&#95;-&#95;Hummel&#95;-&#95;1943&#95;-&#95;Vol.&#95;2.pdf/268\"><span id=\"pageindex&#95;268\" class=\"pagenum-inner ws-noexport\">&#8203;</span></span></span><b>WU</b> J\u00ean-ch'\u00ean \u5433\u4efb\u81e3 (<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r14767791\">.mw-parser-output .wst-tooltip{cursor:help;border-bottom:thin dotted cornflowerblue}.mw-parser-output .wst-tooltip-nodash{border-bottom:none}</style><span class=\"wst-tooltip wst-tooltip-dash\" title=\"Courtesy name (Tz\u00fb/Zi, \u5b57)\">T.</span>&#160;\u5fd7\u4f0a, \u723e\u5668, \u5f81\u9d3b,&#32;<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r14767791\" /><span class=\"wst-tooltip wst-tooltip-dash\" title=\"Literary name (Hao, \u865f)\">H.</span>&#160;\u8a17\u5712), 1628?\u20131689?, historian and mathematician, was a native of J\u00ean-ho (Hangchow), Chekiang. Because of his achievements in the field of historical scholarship he was recommended in 1678 to take the special examination known as <i>po-hs\u00fceh hung-tz'\u016d</i> (see under <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/P%27%C3%AAng_Sun-y%C3%BC\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/P&#39;\u00eang Sun-y\u00fc\">P'\u00eang Sun-y\u00fc</a></span>) which he passed in the ensuing year. He was thereupon made a corrector in the Hanlin Academy, assigned to the compilation of the official Ming history (<i>Ming-shih</i>). The section of that history which deals with the calendar was primarily his contribution, and differs from similar sections in preceding dynastic histories in giving diagrams. Wu J\u00ean-ch'\u00ean directed his studies to various fields, writing treatises on the Rites, on the calendar of the <i><a href=\"/wiki/Spring_and_Autumn_Annals\" class=\"mw-redirect mw-disambig\" title=\"Spring and Autumn Annals\">Spring and Autumn Annals</a></i> and on etymology. But his best known works are the \u5341\u570b\u6625\u79cb <i>Shih-kuo ch'un-ch'iu</i>, first printed in 1678 in 114 <i>ch\u00fcan</i>; and the \u5c71\u6d77\u7d93\u5ee3\u8a3b <i>Shan-hai ching kuang-chu</i>, printed for the first time in 1667, in 18 <i>ch\u00fcan</i>. The former is a history of the ten kingdoms which flourished from 902 to 979 A.D. during the period of transition between the Tang and the Sung dynasties. The latter is an amplification of an ancient commentary to the <i><a href=\"https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E5%B1%B1%E6%B5%B7%E7%B6%93\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"zh:\u5c71\u6d77\u7d93\">Shan-hai ching</a></i>\u2014a commentary prepared, early in the fourth century, by Kuo P'u (see under <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Ku_Kuang-ch%27i\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Ku Kuang-ch&#39;i\">Ku Kuang-ch'i</a></span>). Both works were given descriptive notice in the <i>Imperial Catalogue</i> and both were copied into the Imperial Library (see under <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Chi_Y%C3%BCn\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Chi Y\u00fcn\">Chi Y\u00fcn</a></span>).\n</p>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r15431518\">.mw-parser-output .wst-rule{background-color:currentcolor;color:inherit;width:auto;margin:2px auto 2px auto;height:1px;overflow:hidden}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.wst-rule-left{margin-left:0}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.wst-rule-right{margin-right:0}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.__uirule{background-color:#a2a9b1;color:inherit;border:0;margin-top:0.2em;margin-bottom:0.2em}</style><hr class=\"wst-rule wst-rule-left\" style=\"color:inherit;width:40%;\" />\n<p>[2/68/2b; 16/14/25a; 17/2/16b; 30/2/19a; 32/3/22b; <i>Hangchow fu-chih</i> (1922) 145/15a; <i>Wu-lin ts'ang-shu lu</i> (see under <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Ting_Ping\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Ting Ping\">Ting Ping</a></span>) <i>hsia</i> 2b; <i>Ss\u016d-k'u</i> 66/7a, 142/1a; <i>Chou-j\u00ean chuan</i> (see under <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Juan_Y%C3%BCan\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Juan Y\u00fcan\">Juan Y\u00fcan</a></span>) 3d series 1/1a in <i>Nan-ch'ing shu-y\u00fcan ts'ung-shu</i> (see under <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Huang_T%27i-fang\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Huang T&#39;i-fang\">Huang T'i-fang</a></span>).]\n</p>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r15431519\">.mw-parser-output .wst-right{text-align:right}</style><div class=\"wst-right\" style=\"margin-right:2em;\">\n<p><span class=\"smallcaps\" style=\"font-variant:small-caps;\">Tu Lien-ch\u00ea</span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<p><br />\n&#32;\n</p>\n</div>\n</div>"},"links":[{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Chi Y\u00fcn"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Huang T'i-fang"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Juan Y\u00fcan"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Ku Kuang-ch'i"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/P'\u00eang Sun-y\u00fc"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Ting Ping"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Wu I"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Wu Ju-lun"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Spring and Autumn Annals"},{"ns":102,"exists":"","*":"Author:Arthur W. Hummel"},{"ns":102,"exists":"","*":"Author:Tu Lien-ch\u00ea"}],"sections":[],"wikitext":{"*":"{{Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period\n | volume   = 2\n | onlysection = wu jen-ch'en\n | previous = Wu I\n | next     = Wu Ju-lun\n | from     = 268\n | to       = 268\n | notes    =\n | section_author = Tu Lien-ch\u00ea\n}}{{DEFAULTSORT:Wu J\u00ean-ch'\u00ean}}"}}}